# AIDE rules for system-scope file integrity monitoring on Guix System.
# Read through the aide.conf that aide-service-type generates, which supplies
# database_in, database_out and report_url.
#
# NB1: AIDE 0.19 requires each rule line to start with a literal '/' — a
#      leading regex like `.*` is not allowed. A regex *after* the leading
#      slash is fine, so `/(root|home/[^/]+)/...` covers root plus any single
#      user home directory in one rule.
#
# NB2: Guix populates /etc mostly with symlinks into /gnu/store/... whose
#      targets churn on every reconfigure, producing constant noise. Symlinks
#      are dropped except for a short list where a repoint would be an auth
#      bypass; those do show a diff when a reconfigure changes them.
#
# NB3: a negative rule beats an overlapping positive one whatever the order or
#      specificity (checked against 0.19.3), so the exceptions have to live
#      inside the negative as a lookahead. Needs a PCRE-capable AIDE.

# Rule groups
# p     = permissions      u = user    g = group
# ftype = file type        l = link target (symlinks only)
# sha512 = content hash (regular files only)
#
# No mtime/ctime/size — dir/symlink churn produces noise; sha512 covers
# content for regular files.
NORMAL = p+u+g+ftype+sha512+l

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and keys — root's plus every user's ~/.ssh and ~/.gnupg. Watch
# EVERYTHING including symlinks, since a symlink appearing in a credential dir
# would itself be a red flag. /home/[^/]+ matches any single user home.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.ssh($|/) NORMAL
/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg($|/) NORMAL
# Exclude gnupg runtime/ephemeral noise
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/random_seed$
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/\.#.*
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/S\..*
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/log-.*
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/crls\.d($|/)
!/(root|home/[^/]+)/\.gnupg/openpgp-revocs\.d($|/)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /etc — real files (passwd/shadow/group/machine-id etc.), plus the few
# symlinks below whose target is worth watching.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/etc($|/) NORMAL
# Auth stack, identity resolution, login-time code execution, authorization
# rules, trust stores, root code-execution paths. $-anchored: only the
# top-level entry, so /etc/ssl/certs below stays excluded.
!/etc/(?!(pam\.d|security|nsswitch\.conf|profile|bashrc|bashrc\.d|environment|login\.defs|shells|polkit-1|dbus-1|ssl|containers|modprobe\.d|udev)$).* l
!/etc/resolv\.conf$
!/etc/mtab$
!/etc/blkid\.tab.*
!/etc/ssl/certs($|/)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /boot — kernel, initrd, bootloader.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/boot($|/) NORMAL
